## 3. Storage Architecture & Auto-Initialization

### Zero Codebase Pollution (AppData Shadow Workspace)
When `codeless` starts in any workspace, it calculates the project's SHA-256 hash of the canonical root path and **automatically bootstraps** `~/.codeless/projects/<project_hash>/abb_workspace/` from the vendored template (`templates/agent_buildable_base/`) if it does not already exist. The template version (`VERSION`) and a min-compatible version are recorded in `metadata.json` (see A7).

**Dev-mode override (for dogfooding, §12):** if `<repo>/.codeless/abb_workspace/` exists, it takes precedence over AppData. Directory is gitignored by default.

```
[User Machine Home]
├── ~/.codeless/
│   ├── settings.json                   # Global config (upstream multi-layer system, renamed)
│   ├── mcp.json                        # Global MCP servers (upstream mcp config, renamed)
