## 5. Tool Model: ABB Workflows ↔ Upstream Tools

No tool renames (C1). The bridge only adds **path virtualization** to existing file tools and **hooks** to existing write tools.

| ABB workflow capability (as written in ABB docs) | Upstream tool used | Bridge behavior |
|---|---|---|
| "File Content Review" / reading workflows, tasks, references | `Read`, `Glob` | ABB paths resolve to shadow workspace; code paths resolve to repo root (A3). |
| Creating tasks, designs, features, source files | `Write` | `PreToolUse` hook: frontmatter schema validation for ABB files (A1). |
| "Locate Checklist Progress" / updating `[ ]`→`[/]`→`[x]` | `Edit` | `PreToolUse`/`PostToolUse` hooks: DAG gate, status sync, two-track verify, roll-up (§7). |
| Non-contiguous edits | `MultiEdit` (or repeated `Edit`) | Same hooks as `Edit`. |
| "Workspace Text Grep" / "Global Symbol Search" | `Grep`, `Glob`, `LSP` tool | Search roots = repo root + shadow workspace. |
| "Environment Test Execution", lint, git diff | `Bash` | Permission-checked; `PostToolUse` on verify commands feeds the `[x]` gate. |
| "Ask user" (user_input.md) | `AskUser` | ABB change A6 aligns question schema. |
| Background/long-running work | `Job*` tools (renamed from `Task*`, C3) | Unchanged semantics. |
| Subagent dispatch | `Agent`, `SendMessage`, `TeamCreate/Delete` | Worker sandboxing per §10. |
| External systems | `MCPTool`, `ListMcpResources`, `ReadMcpResource` | Unchanged. |
| Mode switching | `EnterPlanMode`, `ExitPlanMode` | Backing primitives for Tri-Mode (§9). |

