## 6. How ABB Workflows Are Executed

| Workflow File | How Codeless Executes It |
|---|---|
| `agent.md` + `workflows/router.md` | Auto-injected at session start by the **ABB Prompt Injector** via upstream's prompt-assembly/CLAUDE.md-style injection mechanism (not a new system). Model classifies intent, then `Read`s the target workflow. A5 adds an optional `ROUTE: <id>` audit line. |
| `planning/init_project.md` | Model detects/asks stack via `AskUser`, fills `STACK.md` (including verification manifest, A2), creates `goal.md` + initial base tasks from `_templates/`. |
| `planning/planning.md` | Research (`Read`, `Grep`), options via `AskUser`, writes to `design/`. |
| `tasks/tasks.md` | Model copies `_templates/sub.md` via `Write`; hooks validate frontmatter + `depends_on`. |
| `execution/work_principle.md` | Model implements active `tasks/sub/NN_task.md` in the **codebase root** (A3), minimal diffs. |
| `execution/work_verification.md` | Model runs Track 1 + Track 2 via `Bash`; the `PostToolUse` verify hook hard-gates the `[x]` transition (§7). |
| `skills/manage_skills.md` | Pull-adapt-delete: clone into `skills/_staging/`, adapt, register in `skills.md` (+ machine-readable index, A4), purge `_staging/` (enforced by `PreSkillImport` hook). |
| `references/references.md` | On-demand `Read`/`Grep` against the 11-domain memory bank. |
| `quality/fallback_policy.md` | No blanket `try/except` unless user requests; surfaced in prompt injection. |
| `skills/debug/traceback` | On test failure: inspect `logs/failure/`, find root frame, write regression test. |
| `ci/setup_ci.md` | Model scaffolds GitHub Actions per `STACK.md`. |

