## 10. Subagent Workers (Max 3 Concurrent)

Per `workflows/execution/work_principle.md`, using upstream `coordinator/` (Agent tool + headless worker mode) — no new swarm engine:
- Supervisor detects subtasks with all `depends_on` satisfied → dispatches up to **3 concurrent headless workers** (cap enforced in coordinator config).
- **Context sandboxing**: each worker receives exactly (1) target subtask file, (2) its frontmatter `links`, (3) referenced `references/` snippets, (4) assigned skill bodies (A1 `skills:` field).
- Workers execute edits + two-track verification and report structured diffs/test output to the supervisor.
- Phase 2 concurrency test: dispatch 5 ready subtasks, assert ≤3 run concurrently.

