## 11. Required ABB Changes (work items in `AkshatTilak/agent_buildable_base`)

These are changes to the ABB repo itself so the harness can be deterministic. Each is independently shippable and backward-compatible with standalone ABB use.

### 11.1. ABB Branch Model (D4 — branch-dependent tracking)
| Branch | Purpose | Consumed by |
|---|---|---|
| `main` | **The branch Codeless itself uses.** Generic ABB scaffold and the vendored template the harness ships (`templates/agent_buildable_base/` submodule → `main`). Also what any standalone ABB user consumes. | Codeless repo (submodule pin), standalone ABB users |
| `codeless` | **Tracking branch for our project.** All harness-driven ABB work is developed and tracked here first: A1–A8 (machine-readable status, verification manifest, `CODEBASE_ROOT`, YAML skill index, …), plus any future schema changes our project needs. | Development/staging only — nothing ships directly from it |

Rules:
- `codeless` branch is created from `main`; it stays rebased/merged forward from `main` as the scaffold evolves.
- **Promotion flow**: changes are developed and dogfood-validated on `codeless`, then promoted (merged) into `main` — because Codeless itself must use `main` (D4). Promotion is a deliberate merge per change (or batch), so `main` only ever receives validated improvements. Since we own ABB (D5), generic changes like A1–A3 are expected to be promoted quickly.
- The submodule in the Codeless repo points at **`main`**; during early development (before A1–A3 are promoted) the dogfood workspace (§12) may temporarily seed from the `codeless` branch via the dev-mode override, switching to `main` once promoted.
- `metadata.json` records which ABB branch + commit the shadow workspace was bootstrapped from (A7).

### 11.2. Change List
| # | Change | Why the harness needs it | Files touched |
|---|---|---|---|
| **A1** ✅ | Add machine-readable task state to frontmatter: `status: pending \| in_progress \| done \| blocked`, plus `complexity:` (from `tasks.md` §5 rubric) and `skills:` list. Rule: **frontmatter is source of truth**; harness syncs body checkboxes from it. *(Confirmed by D5 — we own ABB and will change it.)* | Hooks cannot reliably regex body checkboxes (C9). Subagent packaging needs `complexity`/`skills` without prose parsing. | `tasks/_templates/*.md`, `tasks/tasks.md`, `agent.md` §4 |
| **A2** | Add a **verification manifest**: YAML block in `STACK.md` frontmatter (or `references/tests/verification.md`) with `track_1: [cmds]`, `track_2: [cmds]`, `lint:`, `typecheck:`. | TwoTrackVerifyHook must execute tests deterministically, not parse prose (C11). | `STACK.md`, `workflows/planning/init_project.md` (to populate it), `workflows/execution/work_verification.md` §3 |
| **A3** | Introduce path variables: `ABB_ROOT` (where tasks/references live) and `CODEBASE_ROOT` (where source lives). Workflows reference code via `CODEBASE_ROOT`. Standalone ABB: both equal project root. Under Codeless: ABB_ROOT=shadow, CODEBASE_ROOT=repo. | ABB currently assumes code is co-located with the ABB tree — false under shadow virtualization (C10). | `agent.md`, `workflows/execution/work_principle.md`, `workflows/planning/init_project.md`, templates |
| **A4** | Make `skills/skills.md` dual-format: keep the human table, add a machine-readable YAML index (`name`, `path`, `description`, `version`). | SkillBridge registers ABB skills into the upstream skill loader without prose parsing; also handles ABB's **nested category layout** vs upstream's flat expectation. | `skills/skills.md`, `skills/manage_skills.md` |
| **A5** | Router audit contract: after classification, model emits `ROUTE: <workflow_id>` before reading the workflow. | Lets the harness log/audit routing decisions and power the TUI "active workflow" indicator. Optional but cheap. | `workflows/router.md` |
| **A6** | Align `user_input.md` question format with the harness `AskUser` tool schema (options list, recommended flag, freeform toggle). | Guarantees structured interactive prompts instead of plain-text questions. | `workflows/user/user_input.md` |
